# View of GambitDarwinAcceleration::directSourceContract; historical all3 evidence is separate.
direction: down
source: "Clean master f1c787; zero overlays\nSame authoritative source for all phases"
profile: "Darwin task: build-process concurrency\nSINGLE_VM / SINGLE_THREADED_VMS / disable-smp\nNo native-SMP or multiple-VM prerequisite"
producer: "Existing typed Python + Bazel source producer\nSame configure and ordered stage calls; one deadline\n8GiB charged-footprint guard; RSS observation only\nNo heap/p1 override"
correspondence: "CI Git-bound correspondence\n8 upstream files equal; 9 support inputs inventoried\nEffective source / SDK / RAM equivalence still open"
compiler: "Full branch compiler and original tools\nDefault startup + continuation/GC core smoke\nNo Homebrew or incomplete-prefix substitution"
refusal: "Actual baseline: core and Gerbil main passed\nSupervisor stops at sum-RSS 8.33GiB\nShared mappings not deduplicated; not physical RAM\nNo kernel OOM or CI failure established"
loader: "Historical import stack: 849/864 samples\ndlopen -> dyld mapSegments -> fcntl\nOne-second sample; whole-run time unresolved"
products: "Phase products + ordered LinkPlan\nRemove repeated generation/compile work\nBounded external GSC/GCC jobs"
packages: "MCP AND POO\ngerbil clean / build / original tests\nMatched baseline and candidate"
net: "Cold and incremental net benefit\nDeduct existing optimizations\n2x target remains unmeasured"
ownership: "SysML owns runtime/build distinction\nASCENT enforces source/profile ownership\nQNT readiness/history; Lean semantic/ABI refinement"
source -> profile -> producer -> compiler -> products -> packages -> net
ownership -> producer
ownership -> products
